# Homepage & Layout Design Improvements
**Date:** 2026-05-04  
**Files Modified:** `src/pages/HomePage.jsx`, `src/components/Layout.jsx`

---

## Overview

This session focused on a design critique and overhaul of the homepage and layout component. The goal was to move the UI from a rough "work in progress" feel to a polished, professional standard — with particular attention to the "Why Learn With Us?" section, which had structural and visual issues.

---

## Issues Identified

### `HomePage.jsx`

| # | Issue | Location |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `font-mono` applied to root div conflicted with `font-sans` in Layout, making body text look like code | Line 31 |
| 2 | "Why Learn With Us?" used a single `<p>` block with `<br/>` separators for 4 distinct points — looked like a wall of text | Lines 122–127 |
| 3 | A numbered `<ul>` below that paragraph listed 3 *different* points — redundant and contradictory | Lines 128–141 |
| 4 | The illustration (`undraw_education_1.png`) was nested inside a stray dashed-border placeholder `<div>` that still rendered its SVG icon | Lines 112–118 |
| 5 | Hero only had one CTA ("View my projects") — missed an obvious "Start Learning" primary action | Lines 47–55 |
| 6 | "Courses" and "My Projects" section headings had no subtitles, making them feel bare | Lines 96–99, 153–156 |

### `Layout.jsx`

| # | Issue | Location |
|---|---|---|
| 7 | Logo and nav links shared the same `flex space-x-2 md:space-x-8` wrapper — cramped on mobile, no visual separation | Line 8 |
| 8 | Nav links used `block` display unnecessarily inside an inline flex row | Lines 17–34 |

